  "clarifications": [
    "Relation descriptor instances selected by `$x[<Relation>, (.Name = NAME)]` are model metadata; applied edges remain `((NAME))` and literals stay literal. Headers intentionally preserve Current Subject notation.",
    "R2475/R2476 preview uses existing R2613 generic `$host`/`$target` endpoint signature only within Relation Declarations, with prose retaining endpoint restrictions. Moving R2476 signature from #instances to #model must be explicitly reviewed as a signature, not an instance fact.",
    "R2617 retains the same inverse direction `<((HAS_INVERSE))`; / remains CONTAINS alias.",
    "R2720 uses only alias($r) bound-Relation operand; formal Operator//Alias descriptor remains held pending shared Operator addressing."
  ],
  "blockers": [
    "R2780/R2781 `Operator//Narrowing` and `Operator//Containment`, and R2720 `Operator//Alias` remain in bodies unchanged: targeted Current scan found no declaration of Operator.Name or approved filter addressing Operator descriptors. Replacing with an invented `.Name` or treating an Operator as Relation would be unsound.",
    "These previews do not solve Subject metadata migration, named-instance collision outside their bodies, or / and // transition. Coordinate all mutually dependent syntax changes and exact pins.",
    "R2720 and three Relation previews require atomic acceptance and coordinated typed-notation migration; existing `Relation//NAME` operator metadata and Subject headers are transitional."
  ],
  "boundary": "Preview-only; no native Draft, Current, code, tests, Workflow/Workbench or Git modifications."
}
